From: HardDinD developers
Subject: [EXPERIMENT] um: borrow a parked runner's FP image until a consumer

Standalone, default off: uml_fp_lazy=1. Parallel x86-64 SIGSYS only; lifecycle and
sigreturn and boot-time register discovery retain eager copies. The complete validated standard xstate image
stays authoritative in the parked runner. Reuse it only for the same image on
return. Materialize before switching away, duplicating a task, exporting or
editing FP regsets, or constructing/restoring a signal frame. Exec discards the
old image. Recheck lifecycle numbers after ptrace; discard pending state on
a final switch after exit_mm (including fatal seccomp). Materialization cannot schedule while copying, since a switch may
reuse the runner. This does not alter XSAVE masks, layout, host signal delivery,
or architectural FP state. No XINUSE or syscall-purity approximation is used.
/proc/uml_fp_lazy counts borrowed, reused and materialized images per machine.
When profiling, apply after fault-rendezvous-counters and core-syscall-profile.
Do not combine with core-fp-compare (both replace the same restoration copy).

